                        {
                            "text": "4th councillor jobs [6] :",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Chancellor - Perform Statecraft : increases threat decay speed, and can fire events which improve relations with random vassals, neighbours, or liege.",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Marshal - Organize the Army : lowers the upkeep cost of retinue (or horde), and can fire events to train existing or find new commander",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Steward - Administer Realm : increases the speed of cultural conversion in realm provinces, and can fire events adding economic bonuses to any province.",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Spymaster - Sabotage : target province will suffer damage, gain unrest, and may even be made easier to siege.",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Court Chaplain - Hunt Heretics :  hunts for members of secret societies.",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Artifacts and relics [7] : commissioning swords from skilled smiths, buying fabulous Crown Jewels, hunting for Holy Artifacts.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Allies in Wars: a player can command its allies in a war, ordering them to hunt for enemy armies, to siege strongholds (either by itself or a specific province), or attach them to a specific army. [8]",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Prisoner mass actions (release, ransom, or execute all)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Ability to randomize the name of newborn children (after a parent, a grand-parent, a random ancestor or a random cultural name)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Two sets of portraits and units for Norman and English cultures, as well as Central Germanic culture group [9] :",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
