        {
            "heading": "Patch features",
            "level": 2,
            "content": []
        },
        {
            "heading": "Secret cults",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Almost all of the main (non-heretic) religions have a corresponding \"secret cult\", consisting of followers who falsely profess faith in one religion while secretly belonging to another. [10]"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Members get missions and powers to induce Sympathy for their real religion in other characters in the realm as well as the population in the counties",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "At the highest rank, the ruler can overtly embrace the religion and convert. With careful groundwork, an extremely powerful religious revolt can be staged.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note: You may only form a Secret Cult as a pagan if the religion has already been reformed."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Quality of life changes",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Intrigue screen [11] :"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "New decisions menu showing 6 decisions at once, rather than the old 4.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Ability to mark a decision as important or not, which will trigger its alerts",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "New tab My Plots , showing clearly who the target of each backed plot is",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "New buttons in Known Plots tab, to ask the plotter to end their plot, and ask to join to a plot",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Improved events now showing the targets of plot when invited to join, or option to keep a plot secret when a plotter tries and fails to kill your spymaster due to them discovering their plot.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Other changes [12] :"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Battle indicator showing whenever a unit entering a province (or two units, if they’re entering the same province) will cause a battle to occur.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Garrison tooltip showing levy, and the garrison+levy numbers",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "\"Embark All\" button for when having multiple units selected",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Game rules categories and four save slots allowing to have different pre-sets of rules.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Character finder reset filter, configuration pre-sets, filter by diplomatic range, filter by joining your court",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Councilor selection screen with voting pattern indicators",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Ask the Council to consider a vote before actually voting on it, which allows it to be shown on the Council screen along with icons on each Councilor showing how they will vote.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Childhood education screen will now show which traits the child has got that positively or negatively influence the different education choices",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Commander auto-assignment checkbox",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Map fixes",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Most hideous offenders on the map have been fixed [13] , in particular:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Ural mountains",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Lake Baikal",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The Ganges river",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Kingdom of Cumania de jure changes",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Kingdom of Greece and Kingdom of Trebizond de jure changes",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Hungary and the Danube",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Misc",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Treasury system to see a character’s items as physical objects, and allowing items to be inheritable and stealable. Some existing character modifiers from events will be converted into items, such as the +1 axe, the saint’s bones, or the trophy made from the skull of a rival.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Adjustment of audio volume for all audio assets (ambient sound effects are lower in the background until zooming in, interface sound effects do not interrupt the music, ...) [14]",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Trivia",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Monks and Mystics was the second and final DLC with David \"Darkrenown\" Ballantyne as Game Designer."
                }
            ]
        },
